(5491344, 790233, 83313, '<td valign="top">Heavy compression artifacts and a resulting loss of smoothness and detail are really hurting an entry that I would otherwise give a pretty good vote to. Check your compression settings when you save your file. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (150k for this one)</td>', 'Heavy compression artifacts and a resulting loss of smoothness and detail are really hurting an entry that I would otherwise give a pretty good vote to. Check your compression settings when you save your file. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (150k for this one)', '2009-05-18 14:16:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5491347, 789511, 83313, '<td valign="top">I like the sentiment, but I don''t think this is something that would be found hanging on a corporate wall to motivate employees. The photo seems a bit odd as well, being cropped pretty tight and with that flagpole down the middle.</td>', 'I like the sentiment, but I don''t think this is something that would be found hanging on a corporate wall to motivate employees. The photo seems a bit odd as well, being cropped pretty tight and with that flagpole down the middle.', '2009-05-18 14:18:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5491421, 790646, 103601, '<td valign="top">this is an awesome image, excellent work. one thing to look out for, there are very noticeable halos around their heads, probably from a little too much sharpening. it''s something i do myself all the time. in advanced, you could probably clone it out and be fine, but for basic editing, i''m not sure of a way to remove them. you might be able to get away with a little less sharpening next time. still, an 8 from me :)</td>', 'this is an awesome image, excellent work. one thing to look out for, there are very noticeable halos around their heads, probably from a little too much sharpening. it''s something i do myself all the time. in advanced, you could probably clone it out and be fine, but for basic editing, i''m not sure of a way to remove them. you might be able to get away with a little less sharpening next time. still, an 8 from me :)', '2009-05-18 15:41:59.000000', NULL, 1),
