(5493484, 790660, 96721, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kbhatia1967:</b></div><hr/><i> To me, the colors are too much saturated. This is called OVER-PROCESSING. Sorry for being rude, but someone had to tell you this. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>For somebody with a highest scoring shot that is so oversaturated in reds that detail is all but lost and also as someone supposedly able to teach the art of photoshop enough to author a booklet on the subject, I find this beyond rude...<br/> <br/>Good shot and nice to see you improving with those new lights, keep it up the 6+ is around the corner.<br/> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-05-20 03:23:49.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by kbhatia1967: To me, the colors are too much saturated. This is called OVER-PROCESSING. Sorry for being rude, but someone had to tell you this.   For somebody with a highest scoring shot that is so oversaturated in reds that detail is all but lost and also as someone supposedly able to teach the art of photoshop enough to author a booklet on the subject, I find this beyond rude... Good shot and nice to see you improving with those new lights, keep it up the 6+ is around the corner. ', '2009-05-20 04:22:51.000000', '2009-05-20 04:23:49.000000', 0),
